      span.eyebrow My path
      h2 From early systems work to full product ownership.
    div.prose
      section
        h3 Engineering across eras
        p My career began with PHP, Python, Perl, C++, Microsoft SQL Server, and a small development agency. That broad foundation grew into deep Ruby on Rails experience and, later, Elixir, Phoenix, LiveView, modern JavaScript, and mobile products.
      section
        h3 Product-minded work
        p I care about the user workflow, the data model, the operational constraints, and the team that must live with the code. Architecture is useful when it helps the product adapt—not when it exists to impress other engineers.
      section
        h3 Learning through independent products
        p Papereg, ResellerIO, Oceanowledge, Texas Heavy, and Eos Learning are how I explore new product domains and own the full delivery loop. They force every architectural idea to meet a real interface, real data, and real maintenance.
      section
        h3 Knowledge should travel
        p I mentor developers, create course material, document patterns, and write about tools and experiments. Clear communication is part of engineering because systems only remain healthy when other people can understand them.
  section.section.shell
    div.section-heading
      div
        span.eyebrow Working principles
        h2 What you can expect from me.
      p These are not abstract values. They are the habits I use to make decisions in production.
    div.panel-grid
      article.panel
        span.panel-index 01
        h3 Make the problem concrete
        p Trace the real workflow, establish evidence, and define the user or operational outcome before reaching for abstractions.
      article.panel
        span.panel-index 02
        h3 Prefer maintainable momentum
        p Ship the smallest complete solution, preserve data and existing behavior, and leave the next engineer a clear path forward.
      article.panel
        span.panel-index 03
        h3 Own verification
        p Tests, browser checks, monitoring, rollback thinking, and honest completion reports belong to the implementation—not after it.
  section.section.shell
    div.quote-card
      blockquote “Clean code matters. Clear decisions and reliable delivery matter more.”
